<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Savaiʻi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Savaiʻi is the largest island of the Samoan archipelago and of the independent state of Samoa, a shield volcano whose last eruptions, from Mount Matavanu in 1905–1911, buried villages in lava. Its high chiefly titles were among the leading titles of Samoa. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> held it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upolu">Upolu</a> as German Samoa from 1900 until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> occupied the colony in 1914.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/savaii.jpg" alt="Savaiʻi" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Telim tor · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samoa_Savaii_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
